        7,
        8,
        9
      ],
      "timers": [
        {
          "text": "4 hours",
          "seconds": 14400
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Make the mac salad first, since it needs to chill: boil 225 g elbow macaroni in water with 1 tbsp salt (for the pasta water) for 2 minutes longer than the package says, until soft. Drain, toss with 2 tbsp cider vinegar, 1 small carrot, finely grated and 1 tbsp grated onion, and cool completely.",
      "ingredientRefs": [
        13,
        14,
        15,
        16,
        17
      ],
      "timers": []
    },
    {
      "text": "Whisk 240 g mayonnaise (Best Foods/Hellmann's), 120 ml whole milk, 1 tsp sugar and 1/2 tsp black pepper (for the salad), fold into the macaroni, season with 1/2 tsp salt, to taste, and refrigerate 4 hours. It will thicken; stir in a splash of milk before serving.",
      "ingredientRefs": [
        18,
        19,
        20,
        21,
        22
      ],
      "timers": [
        {
          "text": "4 hours",
          "seconds": 14400
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Simmer the reserved marinade in a small pan for 3 minutes, until slightly syrupy.",
      "ingredientRefs": [],
      "timers": [
        {
          "text": "3 minutes",
          "seconds": 180
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Heat 1 tbsp neutral oil in a cast-iron pan or griddle over high. Shake excess marinade off the beef and sear in batches, 1 minute per side, until caramelized at the edges.",
      "ingredientRefs": [
        10
      ],
      "timers": [
        {
          "text": "1 minute",
          "seconds": 60
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Brush the beef with the glaze, scatter with 2 scallions, sliced and 1 tsp toasted sesame seeds, and plate with two scoops of 900 g hot cooked white rice and one scoop of mac salad.",
