  "notes": "Mac salad is meant to be soft and creamy, not al dente: overcooking the pasta and dressing it with vinegar while hot lets it absorb the dressing. Plain mayo and milk only; no mustard, relish or celery in the classic plate-lunch version.\n\nGrilling over charcoal is the other traditional way: 2 minutes per side over high heat.",
